    thinking: "**Defining Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m defining the project scope based on the user\'s request. Focusing on user authentication via sign-in, I\'m now outlining the expected user flow and integrating Gemini API with Firestore. The initial focus is on the landing page and the sign-in prompt. I need to clarify user actions post-authentication.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nNow I\'m expanding the project\'s feature set. The user\'s dashboard will enable multi-turn journal entries and interactions with Gemini for helpful summaries and reflections. All user interactions will be saved to Firestore, ensuring strict user isolation. The system will also provide the user with a view of their past entries. I am now working on integration of these new features.\n\n\n\n**Prioritizing Security Measures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on security protocols. I\'m focusing on server-side API endpoints for the Gemini interaction, specifically `/api/gemini/reflect` and `/api/gemini/summarize`. This means the API key is completely protected on the server. I also want to make sure I map the data flow, validate the access control, and prepare a severity-ranked vulnerability list and remediations.\n\n\n"
