  planner_response {
    response: "### Security & Threat Analysis Summary\n\n| Threat Zone | Identified Scenario / Risk | OWASP Vector | Countermeasure / Mitigation Implemented |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Input Surfaces** | Malicious prompt injections & payload buffer overruns | OWASP LLM02 / A03 | 10MB request payload guard, defensive null-safe destructuring, and message sanitization prior to Gemini inference. |\n| **2. Planning & Reasoning** | System prompt override attempts to extract internal instructions or secrets | OWASP LLM01 | Strict system instruction role binding on server-side `@google/genai` calls; user content treated strictly as plain input. |\n| **3. Tool Execution** | Rate limits or model degradation causing application outage | OWASP LLM04 / A05 | Automated 4-tier Fallback Ladder (`gemini-3.6-flash` &rarr; `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` &rarr; `gemini-flash-latest` &rarr; `gemini-3.7-flash`). |\n| **4. Memory & State** | Cross-user data leakage or unauthorized document tampering in Firestore | OWASP A01 | Owner-bound Firestore Security Rules enforcing `request.auth.uid == userId` on `/users/{userId}/...` path partitions. Zero insecure defaults. |\n| **5. Inter-System Communication** | Exposure of `GEMINI_API_KEY` in browser network inspect tools | OWASP A02 | Server-side Express API proxy (`/api/gemini/*`). Sensitive credentials remain isolated on the server runtime. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Implementations\n\n- **Federated Google Authentication**: Integrated Firebase Auth with Google Sign-In popups, eliminating local password handling.\n- **User-Isolated Cloud Firestore**: Deployed owner-bound Firestore security rules ensuring each user\'s reflections and multi-turn conversations are partitioned under `/users/{userId}/entries/{entryId}`.\n- **Resilient Multi-Turn Gemini 3.6 Flash Studio**: Built an Express backend proxy featuring an automated model fallback ladder, defensive request payload handling, and markdown formatting.\n- **AI Executive Summarization & Takeaway Extraction**: Integrated structured cognitive synthesis to extract 3\342\200\2236 word titles, executive summaries, core insights, and interactive checklists.\n- **Cognitive Reframing & Brainstorming Tool**: Equipped the studio with 4 exploratory perspective modes: *Cognitive Reframe*, *Micro Action Steps*, *Philosophical Wisdom*, and *Divergent Possibilities*.\n- **Zero-Crash Payload Hygiene**: Implemented recursive undefined-stripping utilities before any Firestore persistence operations.\n- **Production README & Cloud Run Challenge Labeling**: Authored a complete `README.md` with Secret Manager bindings, IAM configurations, and the required deployment label (`dev-tutorial=cloud-run-ai-challenge`).\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Functional Verification Walkthrough\n\n1. **Authentication Flow**: Click **\"Sign in with Google\"** on the landing page &rarr; complete the OAuth popup &rarr; verify the user profile initializes in Firestore at `/users/{uid}`.\n2. **Multi-Turn Reflection Dialogue**: Type your thoughts in the reflection editor &rarr; send a prompt to Gemini &rarr; verify that structured replies with markdown formatting appear and conversation turns persist into Cloud Firestore.\n3. **AI Summarization & Takeaways**: Click **\"Auto-Summarize\"** &rarr; verify Gemini generates an executive summary, mood tag, key takeaways, and an actionable checklist with toggleable completion states.\n4. **Cognitive Brainstorming**: Select **\"Brainstorm & Reframe\"** &rarr; pick a perspective lens (such as *Cognitive Reframe* or *Micro Action Steps*) &rarr; click **\"Generate Structured Perspectives\"** to view tailored guidance.\n5. **History & Isolation Verification**: Create multiple reflections &rarr; use the sidebar search and mood filter pills to navigate past sessions &rarr; confirm that records remain strictly partitioned by user UID."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Directives**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the production build succeeded without errors, which is a relief. Now, I\'m focusing on the project directives, specifically the required Threat Summary Table mapping threat zones to countermeasures as part of Agentic Threat Modeling and the Secure Coding Standard, focused on OWASP A03 / LLM02, LLM01.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Security & Threat Analysis Summary\n\n| Threat Zone | Identified Scenario / Risk | OWASP Vector | Countermeasure / Mitigation Implemented |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Input Surfaces** | Malicious prompt injections & payload buffer overruns | OWASP LLM02 / A03 | 10MB request payload guard, defensive null-safe destructuring, and message sanitization prior to Gemini inference. |\n| **2. Planning & Reasoning** | System prompt override attempts to extract internal instructions or secrets | OWASP LLM01 | Strict system instruction role binding on server-side `@google/genai` calls; user content treated strictly as plain input. |\n| **3. Tool Execution** | Rate limits or model degradation causing application outage | OWASP LLM04 / A05 | Automated 4-tier Fallback Ladder (`gemini-3.6-flash` &rarr; `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` &rarr; `gemini-flash-latest` &rarr; `gemini-3.7-flash`). |\n| **4. Memory & State** | Cross-user data leakage or unauthorized document tampering in Firestore | OWASP A01 | Owner-bound Firestore Security Rules enforcing `request.auth.uid == userId` on `/users/{userId}/...` path partitions. Zero insecure defaults. |\n| **5. Inter-System Communication** | Exposure of `GEMINI_API_KEY` in browser network inspect tools | OWASP A02 | Server-side Express API proxy (`/api/gemini/*`). Sensitive credentials remain isolated on the server runtime. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Architectural Implementations\n\n- **Federated Google Authentication**: Integrated Firebase Auth with Google Sign-In popups, eliminating local password handling.\n- **User-Isolated Cloud Firestore**: Deployed owner-bound Firestore security rules ensuring each user\'s reflections and multi-turn conversations are partitioned under `/users/{userId}/entries/{entryId}`.\n- **Resilient Multi-Turn Gemini 3.6 Flash Studio**: Built an Express backend proxy featuring an automated model fallback ladder, defensive request payload handling, and markdown formatting.\n- **AI Executive Summarization & Takeaway Extraction**: Integrated structured cognitive synthesis to extract 3\342\200\2236 word titles, executive summaries, core insights, and interactive checklists.\n- **Cognitive Reframing & Brainstorming Tool**: Equipped the studio with 4 exploratory perspective modes: *Cognitive Reframe*, *Micro Action Steps*, *Philosophical Wisdom*, and *Divergent Possibilities*.\n- **Zero-Crash Payload Hygiene**: Implemented recursive undefined-stripping utilities before any Firestore persistence operations.\n- **Production README & Cloud Run Challenge Labeling**: Authored a complete `README.md` with Secret Manager bindings, IAM configurations, and the required deployment label (`dev-tutorial=cloud-run-ai-challenge`).\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Functional Verification Walkthrough\n\n1. **Authentication Flow**: Click **\"Sign in with Google\"** on the landing page &rarr; complete the OAuth popup &rarr; verify the user profile initializes in Firestore at `/users/{uid}`.\n2. **Multi-Turn Reflection Dialogue**: Type your thoughts in the reflection editor &rarr; send a prompt to Gemini &rarr; verify that structured replies with markdown formatting appear and conversation turns persist into Cloud Firestore.\n3. **AI Summarization & Takeaways**: Click **\"Auto-Summarize\"** &rarr; verify Gemini generates an executive summary, mood tag, key takeaways, and an actionable checklist with toggleable completion states.\n4. **Cognitive Brainstorming**: Select **\"Brainstorm & Reframe\"** &rarr; pick a perspective lens (such as *Cognitive Reframe* or *Micro Action Steps*) &rarr; click **\"Generate Structured Perspectives\"** to view tailored guidance.\n5. **History & Isolation Verification**: Create multiple reflections &rarr; use the sidebar search and mood filter pills to navigate past sessions &rarr; confirm that records remain strictly partitioned by user UID."
